I agree with you here...just the other day I was in a shop and I
wasn't in a position to steal or buy.  So, just playing around I threw
something in the corner next to the door so that maybe my cat would
pick it up.  Then it dawned on me...the shopkeeper wasn't standing in
front of the door at the moment.  So I tried throwing some shoes out
the door and it worked.  I thought to myself, "Hey this is great!" and
quickly started throwing everything else out the door.  It was a good
thing (sic) that I had a high strength so I could throw that plate
mail 4-5 spaces to make it out the door....

Then I started to leave...you know, just walk out.  I didn't have any
paid items in my pack, so I didn't think twice about being able to
walk on out.  Much to my surprise, the shopkeeper stood in my way!  I
check my packed and I checked it twice...then it dawned on me...the
objects in the corridor which I threw out were unpaid and still
accounted for...damn!  So I tried to start paying with my measly 18gp
and bougth a pair of shoes for 10gp and that was it...pretty much end
of story right there.

Anyway, I guess the point is, that it's obvious that if what I tried
worked, it would have been a major loophole.  Although, I think this
loophole was covered up a loooong time ago...if I were able to do it,
it probably would have made the game less fun in the future.

